Third-party software:

- the binary contains third-party Rust crates and C code compiled by pg_query,
  including libpg_query, PostgreSQL, protobuf-c and xxHash;
- it also contains mimalloc through libmimalloc-sys where enabled; and
- each third-party component remains under its own license.

The container includes:

- the generated compiled-dependency inventory and controlling texts at
  `/usr/share/doc/vericto-proxy/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES`;
- the pinned Chainguard runtime package inventory, source locations and license
  texts at `/usr/share/doc/vericto-proxy/RUNTIME_BASE_LICENSES`; and
- the runtime packages' SPDX documents under `/var/lib/db/sbom`.

`third-party/build-notices.sh` builds `THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES` for the exact Rust
and C dependency graph shipped in the binary. `third-party/runtime-base.txt`
